Data attribution
================

The grade allocations in data/grades.js are transcribed and reformatted from
the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology (MEXT),
Elementary School Course of Study (2017 Notification), Japanese Language,
Appendix: Grade-Based Kanji Allocation Table (学年別漢字配当表).

Source PDF:
https://www.mext.go.jp/content/20220606-mxt_kyoiku02-100002607_002.pdf
Official curriculum page:
https://www.mext.go.jp/a_menu/shotou/new-cs/1384661.htm
MEXT website terms:
https://www.mext.go.jp/b_menu/1351168.htm

The table is based on the 2017 notification and was fully implemented in
Japanese elementary schools from 2020. This package's fixed dataset was
retrieved on 2026-09-29 from PDF pages 195-198 (printed pages 192-195). The
source PDF SHA-256 is
4a18f8d0247415c9e27a86e2688b3759cdb0c032a8e07ab51690a13a5fc27c2e.
The allocation is organized as six JavaScript arrays; no other OSS kanji list
is used as a data source. This package does not claim to be an official MEXT
product or to be maintained by MEXT.

MEXT's website terms permit copying and adaptation with attribution, require
indicating that changes were made, and are compatible with CC BY 4.0. The
dataset is therefore offered under those source terms; this MIT license
applies to the package code only. The code converts the table into a compact
per-grade lookup representation.

Unicode range data
==================

The fixed CJK detection ranges are derived from Unicode 18.0.0,
Unicode Character Database PropList.txt (Unified_Ideograph), together with the
assigned CJK compatibility ideograph ranges in that release:
https://www.unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/ucd/PropList.txt
